      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, economists debate significantly whether increased government spending or market deregulation is the superior tool for fighting inflation. Policies involving increased demand, like government spending, can sometimes fuel further inflation if supply cannot immediately meet that demand. Conversely, market deregulation aims to boost supply elasticity, which proponents argue reduces cost-push inflation. Ultimately, monetary policy adjustments by the central bank often play the most immediate and influential role in curbing current inflationary pressures.",
      "source": "target",
